.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:485:    With these types + traits + Null impls in place, W1-C can compile and test `link::override_link(emitter: &dyn SignalEmitter, ...)` against `NullSignalEmitter` in Wave 1, without referencing any `SignalType` variant (W3-B owns the bus-level emission mapping); W1-B's `open_validated` returns the W1-A-owned `FileIdentity` and `RejectionReason`; W3-A's `WorkspaceExtractor` impl produces W1-A-owned `WorkspaceClaimProposal` records. `mod.rs` declares all submodules with one declaration per line:
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:508:- **Goal:** Migrate the registry of known workspace source types (inbox, Drive, entity-doc, user-attachment, Granola transcript, Quill transcript) to the v1.4.1 `data_source` taxonomy. Establishes the allowlist of file origins the ingestion pipeline accepts and validates paths against. **Cycle 8 amendment (Option B-prime):** also ships `WorkspaceCategoryRegistry` — defines per-entity-type allowed `WorkspaceCategory` values (defaults: `Presentations | Transcripts | Meetings | Notes | Contracts | Attachments`, plus `Other(String)` for extensions registered via the registry) and the path resolution rules: `Accounts/{entity_name}/{category}/{filename}` when category present; `Accounts/{entity_name}/{filename}` when absent (root-level for the entity). Files in `_inbox/` resolve to `_inbox/{filename}` until entity assignment promotes them.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:514:  - Path validation API: `WorkspaceSourceRegistry::open_validated(path) -> Result<(File, FileIdentity), RejectionReason>`. The function canonicalizes the path; confirms the canonical path is a strict child of the configured workspace root; rejects any path containing `..` components even if the canonical form resolves within the workspace; opens the file with `O_NOFOLLOW` (or platform equivalent — `std::os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt::custom_flags(libc::O_NOFOLLOW)` on Unix; corresponding `FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT` semantics on Windows); captures device + inode after open; and returns the open `File` handle plus a `FileIdentity { device, inode, canonical_path }`. **Ingestion code reads from the returned handle — it never re-opens by path.** This closes the validate-then-read TOCTOU race.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:515:  - On rejection, return a typed `RejectionReason { PathTraversalAttempt | SymlinkRefused | SymlinkRaced | OutsideWorkspace }` error to the caller. **W1-B does not emit signals** (cycle 4 amendment to resolve the wave-timing inversion: `WorkspaceFileRejected` SignalType isn't registered until W3-B, so W1-B emitting it directly would not compile in W1). The W2-A pipeline owns signal emission at the boundary based on the typed error variant — `pipeline.rs` calls its `SignalEmitter` slot (constructed via `wiring.rs`) when handling a `RejectionReason` it propagates.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:517:  - Negative fixture suite (per Phase 0 artifact-12 style): TOCTOU race (validate → swap symlink target → attempt read) must produce `RejectionReason::SymlinkRaced`; URL-encoded `%2e%2e`; NFC/NFD Unicode normalization variant of `..`; absolute-path attempts; symlinks pointing outside workspace.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:524:- **Tests required:** All negative fixtures from the security gate (TOCTOU symlink race, `%2e%2e`, NFC/NFD `..`, absolute-path, outside-workspace symlink); valid path acceptance test returning `(File, FileIdentity)`; `DataSource` variant mapping round-trip across all `WorkspaceFileKind` values; CI lint script green (no path-based file reads outside `registry::open_validated`); `cargo clippy -D warnings` clean.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:525:- **Done when:** `WorkspaceSourceRegistry::open_validated` exists and returns `(File, FileIdentity)` from a single atomic open; all negative fixtures rejected with the typed reasons listed in the security gate; CI lint script in place; ingestion call sites in subsequent lanes consume only the returned handle (verified via grep at W2-A merge); migration slot v252 used (cycle 11 renumber); all tests green; `/cso` L0 plan AND L2 diff approval recorded.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:578:- **Goal:** Implement `services::workspace_ingestion::pipeline::IngestPipeline` — the staged pipeline that takes a `(File, FileIdentity)` from `registry::open_validated`, reads content (with sanitization), runs a stub `extract::extract_proposals_*` (W3-A replaces the stub with the real extractor) which returns `Vec::new()` for v1.4.5 W2, records the ingestion run via W1-C tables, and emits lifecycle progress hooks. **W2-A scope is narrowed to a non-claim-producing pipeline shell — no `commit_claim` calls in W2.** Claim production lands in W3-A. Cycle 2 amendment: this resolves the W2-A vs W3-A ownership contradiction (challenge finding #3) and lets DOS-466 land without depending on extraction logic that W3-A owns. W2-A also ships `pipeline::quarantine_source(file_id, reason, actor) -> Result<()>` — the quarantine state mutation that W4-A's source management UI invokes (challenge finding #6). **Cycle 8+9 amendment (Option B-prime):** W2-A also ships `pipeline::auto_detect_category(filename, content_head) -> Option<WorkspaceCategory>` — heuristic detection mined from the archived `prepare_inbox.py`. **Frozen detection rule table (cycle 9 deterministic-contract amendment):**
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:587:  | 1 | Frontmatter field `doc_type` | other registered string | matches `WorkspaceCategoryRegistry` `Other(s)` if present, else None |
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:596:  **Tie-break rules:** higher priority wins; within the same priority, first matched rule wins. **Validation:** auto-detected results MUST pass `WorkspaceCategoryRegistry::validate(category, entity_type)` — if the rule produces a category not allowed for the file's entity type, fall back to `None` (entity root) rather than silently using a disallowed category. **Content sniff bound:** `content_head` is the first 4KB of file content (sufficient for frontmatter parsing); never reads the full file. Pipeline records the resolved category in the lifecycle row and resolves the destination path via `WorkspaceCategoryRegistry` from W1-B.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:605:  - Pipeline reads from the `(File, FileIdentity)` returned by `registry::open_validated` only — never re-opens by path.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:610:  2. *Provenance + trust:* Ingestion run records the `FileIdentity` (device + inode + canonical path) and SHA-256 content hash so W3-A's claim production can attribute correctly.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:615:- **Done when:** `IngestPipeline::run(IngestRequest)` records an ingestion run, transitions lifecycle, and produces zero claim proposals (W3-A's job to land them) where `IngestRequest { file: File, identity: FileIdentity, source_type: SourceType, entity_id: Option<EntityId>, mode: IngestMode, category_hint: Option<WorkspaceCategory> }` (cycle 9 amendment: pipeline accepts a request struct so caller-provided category from DOS-474, W2-C, W2-D, W5-A all flow through). **Cycle 10 contract reconciliation:** `category_hint` is contracted to be a registry-valid `WorkspaceCategory` value when `Some`. Caller-side validation (DOS-474, W2-C, W2-D, W5-A) is responsible for rejecting malformed/disallowed caller-provided slugs BEFORE constructing `IngestRequest` — the pipeline trusts the type. When `category_hint` is `None`, `auto_detect_category()` runs as fallback. The pipeline never sees an "invalid" hint at the type level. `pipeline::quarantine_source` API present and tested; all rejection paths return typed errors; CI lint script `check_workspace_mutation_allowlist.sh` (modeled on `check_claim_writer_allowlist.sh`) green; all tests green; `/cso` L0 plan AND L2 diff approval recorded.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:690:- Stage 3a: **DOS-470 (W3-A) ONLY**. Replaces W2-A's `extract_stub()` with the real `extract_proposals_*` functions and produces the first real `WorkspaceClaimProposal` records via `commit_claim`.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:698:- **Goal:** Extend `services::workspace_ingestion` with the claim extraction logic: given file content (structured JSON/markdown entity files, or extracted text from Drive/attachment files), produce typed `WorkspaceClaimProposal` records (the type is **W1-A-owned in `contracts.rs`** per cycle 6 promotion) using the existing `CLAIM_TYPE_REGISTRY`. This is the "intelligence" half of the ingestion pipeline — converting raw file content to structured claim proposals.
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:777:            { "file_id": String, "data_source_kind": WorkspaceFileKind, "lifecycle_state": LifecycleState, "category": Option<String>, "source_asof": ISO-8601, "attribution_source": String, "confidence": f64, "user_override": Option<{ "actor": String, "at": ISO-8601 }> }
.docs/plans/v1.4.5-waves.md:883:      "category": Option<String>,               // OPTIONAL canonical slug from WorkspaceCategory::as_slug() — one of "presentations" / "transcripts" / "meetings" / "notes" / "contracts" / "attachments" or a registered Other(name) lowercase slug. Cycle 10 contract reconciliation — two distinct branches, no overlap: (a) ABSENT (null/missing): server runs pipeline::auto_detect_category() per the cycle 9 frozen detection rule table; (b) PRESENT: server validates against W1-B WorkspaceCategoryRegistry BEFORE constructing IngestRequest — well-formed AND registry-valid → category_hint = Some(...); malformed OR registry-disallowed → return PlacementError::CategoryNotAllowed and never invoke the pipeline. There is no "invalid hint falls through to auto-detection" path; that behavior would silently bury caller errors.
